Star arguments: every argument of a star builtin may name a variable. One that does is
replaced by that variable's unexpanded value, dedented; one that does not passes as
written, so $(lua* lua.count, words) reads both defines and $(jq.argv* -r, prog, doc)
keeps -r. The argv forms gain twins, and amk.dedent* follows the same rule. A one-argument
import target star still takes its name and body from the one variable.

